   <dc:creator>
    <rdf:Seq>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">Luigi Albert Maria (original)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">adapted under CC BY-SA 4.0</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Seq>
   </dc:creator>
   <dc:title>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">Type I and type II errors in hypothesis testing</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:title>
   <dc:type>
    <rdf:Bag>
     <rdf:li>Text</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Bag>
   </dc:type>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">Three-dimensional diagram of a statistical hypothesis test. A horizontal axis shows values t of the test statistic T</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">and a vertical axis shows the density of T. Two bell-shaped normal density curves of T with the same spread stand on a floor: the density of T under the null hypothesis H0</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">shown in blue on the left</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">and the density of T under the alternative hypothesis H1</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">shown in dark red further to the right and further back. A translucent vertical plane crosses the floor at the critical value c</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">which is marked as a point on the T axis. The plane splits the floor into the acceptance region to the left of c</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">tinted green</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">and the critical region to the right of c</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">tinted orange. The curves are labelled Density of T under H0: f sub T of t given theta0</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">and Density of T under H1: f sub T of t given theta1. The floor regions are labelled Acceptance region (Accept H0) and Critical region (Reject H0). The large part of the H0 curve left of c is labelled 1 minus alpha</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">equal to P(Accept H0 given H0 true). The small tail of the H0 curve to the right of c is labelled alpha equals P(Type I error) equals P(Reject H0 given H0 true). The large part of the H1 curve right of c is labelled 1 minus beta</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">the power</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">equal to P(Reject H0 given H0 false). The small magenta tail of the H1 curve to the left of c is labelled beta equals P(Type II error) equals P(Accept H0 given H0 false). Adapted from &quot;PPV</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">NPV</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">Sensitivity and Specificity&quot; by Luigi Albert Maria</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">Wikimedia Commons</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
   <dc:language>
    <rdf:Bag>
     <rdf:li>en</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Bag>
   </dc:language>
   <dc:date>
    <rdf:Seq>
     <rdf:li>2026-10-29T22:46:35Z</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Seq>
   </dc:date>
